      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level is anchored at April's 544.44 thousand. Momentum is downward because employment strengthened and unemployment declined in May and June. The +2.0-thousand adjustment combines same-month evidence that July 2025 rose 6.6 thousand amid occupational composition effects with an offsetting EI-flow lag: claims entry, return to work, eligibility, and benefit exhaustion need not move contemporaneously with the LFS. No separate policy-change adjustment is applied."
